  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Cronenworth's three-RBI night gave them the room they needed, and the pitching held every inch of it.",
    "what_this_means": "Germ\u00e1n M\u00e1rquez threw five scoreless innings against an Arizona lineup that offered nothing. The bullpen. Matsui, Brito, Rodriguez, and Mason Miller closing it out. Combined to keep the lead intact through all nine. That's the formula when the offense stays thin: pitching has to be perfect, and it was. Campusano went 2-for-3, Cronenworth converted runners, and the Padres took what they built in the first inning and never let it slip. They needed one clean outing. They got four of them. A one-run lead is not a plan, but sometimes a plan is not the point. Execution is. This team doesn't need much. It found enough.",
    "what_to_watch": "Arizona sends Jose Cabrera (4.73 ERA) tonight. Michael King gets the ball for San Diego. Cabrera's walked nearly as many as he's struck out this season. King should have room to work if the lineup can put pressure early.",
